        ["dom-events", "DOM and Events", "Select and update page elements and handle user actions through event listeners.", "Separate data updates from rendering and avoid putting user text into unsafe HTML.", "Build a filterable reading list with add, remove, and search behavior.", [["MDN: Scripting", "https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development/Core/Scripting", "course"]]],
        ["async", "Asynchronous JavaScript and Fetch", "Use promises, async/await, and Fetch to handle work that completes later.", "Show loading and error states and inspect response status before using JSON.", "Load a public JSON dataset and render results with retry and empty states.", [["MDN: Asynchronous JavaScript", "https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development/Extensions/Async_JS", "course"], ["MDN: Fetch API", "https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Fetch_API", "documentation"]]]
